WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.145
What art form is nine hundred years old and includes acrobatics, martial arts, and squeaky singing?

2
00:00:07.146 --> 00:00:10.155
If you guessed the Chinese opera, you're right!

3
00:00:10.156 --> 00:00:17.139
If you're wondering what the Chinese opera is like, and why the singers have squeaky voices, keep reading!

4
00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:21.069
If you were to attend the Chinese opera, this is what it would be like.

5
00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:23.692
First you would see an empty stage.

6
00:00:23.693 --> 00:00:30.131
The actors want people in the audience to use their imagination, so they use only a few stage decorations.

7
00:00:30.132 --> 00:00:36.441
The performers also need a lot of room on stage for their acrobatics and martial arts.

8
00:00:36.442 --> 00:00:38.919
Next you might see a mini orchestra.

9
00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:46.710
The orchestra is usually made up of string instruments like guitars, wind instruments like flutes, drums, and wooden clappers.

10
00:00:46.711 --> 00:00:54.549
These are used to make music as well as sound effects, like a horse galloping or a rooster crowing.

11
00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:57.625
Then you will see the actors come on stage.

12
00:00:57.626 --> 00:01:02.596
There are four groups of characters: Sheng, Dan, Jing, and Chou.

13
00:01:02.597 --> 00:01:06.993
Sheng are the men in the opera, such as an uncle or a little boy.

14
00:01:06.994 --> 00:01:11.829
Unlike the actors in the other three groups, they don't paint their faces.

15
00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:16.701
Dan are the women in the play, and they are the ones who sing with the squeaky voices.

16
00:01:16.702 --> 00:01:21.231
Jing are the warriors or demons. And Chou are the clowns.

17
00:01:21.232 --> 00:01:27.283
They wear white makeup on their noses and their job is to keep the audience laughing.

18
00:01:27.284 --> 00:01:30.920
So why do the Dan sing with squeaky voices?

19
00:01:30.921 --> 00:01:35.689
Even though the Dan are women, the actors playing them are almost always men.

20
00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:40.072
When a man pretends to have a woman's voice, it often sounds squeaky.

21
00:01:40.073 --> 00:01:47.239
Nine hundred years ago, the Chinese opera was performed outside, so the actors had to sing loudly.

22
00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:50.661
Their voices weren't supposed to sound pretty, just loud.

23
00:01:50.662 --> 00:01:54.492
It takes a lifetime of studying to be an actor in the Chinese opera.

24
00:01:54.493 --> 00:01:59.256
Historically, children were sold to the opera to begin training when they were young.

25
00:01:59.257 --> 00:02:03.246
Parents knew that the opera would give their children a good life.

26
00:02:03.247 --> 00:02:10.966
Even though the children were young, they would get up early every morning to begin their exercises, and they would practice all day long.

27
00:02:10.967 --> 00:02:18.885
One actor remembers having to do handstands on a chair for hours and practicing five thousand kicks and punches in one day.

28
00:02:18.886 --> 00:02:25.890
The children were forced to work very hard, but it made their bodies some of the strongest in China.

29
00:02:25.891 --> 00:02:30.037
One of the most famous stars of the Chinese opera is Jackie Chan.

30
00:02:30.038 --> 00:02:35.675
When he was six, his parents signed a ten-year contract so he could be trained in the opera.

31
00:02:35.676 --> 00:02:40.550
When Jackie Chan became an adult, the Chinese opera was not very popular anymore.

32
00:02:40.551 --> 00:02:47.871
So, Jackie Chan used what he had learned at the opera to become one of the best martial arts superstars in movie history.

33
00:02:47.872 --> 00:02:54.767
The Chinese opera is a lot more than beautiful costumes, amazing acrobatics, martial arts stunts, and stories.

34
00:02:54.768 --> 00:03:00.840
It is an art form that brings together the best cultural traditions of China.

